# Kamal reads secrets from this file at deploy time and passes them to the containers as
# environment variables. Every value is pulled from the deploying environment — your shell
# locally, GitHub Actions secrets in CI — so no secret is ever written into an image, and
# nothing sensitive belongs in this file.
#
# This file IS committed. It contains only names, never values. If you ever find yourself
# typing an actual secret to the right of an `=`, stop: that value is going into git.
#
# Generate the four application secrets once, with real entropy:
#
#   openssl rand -base64 48    # JWT_SECRET — must exceed 32 bytes or the API refuses to boot
#   openssl rand -base64 32    # INTERNAL_API_KEY
#   openssl rand -base64 32    # DB_PASSWORD
#   openssl rand -base64 32    # REDIS_PASSWORD
#
# Then store them somewhere durable. DB_PASSWORD in particular cannot simply be changed later:
# it is baked into the Postgres volume on first boot, so rotating it means an ALTER USER inside
# the running container, not an edit here.

KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=$KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD

JWT_SECRET=$JWT_SECRET
INTERNAL_API_KEY=$INTERNAL_API_KEY
DB_PASSWORD=$DB_PASSWORD
REDIS_PASSWORD=$REDIS_PASSWORD

# The Postgres accessory names the same value differently: POSTGRES_PASSWORD is what the image
# reads to create the role, DB_PASSWORD is what Spring reads to connect as it. One secret, two
# names — they must stay equal or the API cannot log in to its own database.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=$DB_PASSWORD

# Likewise for the shared internal key. The API reads INTERNAL_API_KEY; the web app reads it
# under the _SB suffix. Server-rendered requests fail closed if these ever drift apart.
INTERNAL_API_KEY_SB=$INTERNAL_API_KEY

# Cloudflare Origin Certificate, serving the same pair to both services. Generated in the
# Cloudflare dashboard under SSL/TLS -> Origin Server, covering bela.damjan.pro and
# *.bela.damjan.pro, and valid for 15 years.
#
# These are PEM blocks, not single-line values. Set them with:
#   gh secret set CERTIFICATE_PEM --repo damix00/java-bela < origin-cert.pem
#   gh secret set PRIVATE_KEY_PEM --repo damix00/java-bela < origin-key.pem
CERTIFICATE_PEM=$CERTIFICATE_PEM
PRIVATE_KEY_PEM=$PRIVATE_KEY_PEM
